Some exceptions evade to these "rules" in both systems, as inconsistencies appeared throughout updates:
* For {{Pink|RNG Meters}}: in the case of Slayer Bosses, they do not affect the Drop Rates of items in the [[Slayer#Separate Loot Table|Separate Loot Pools]] until the meter is full;
* For {{Pink|Pities}}: in the case of Glacite Mineshafts, they do affect their [[Glacite Mineshafts#Pity|appearance rate]].

==RNG Meter==
The '''{{pink|RNG Meter}}''' is a mechanic that translates the time and efforts spent in certain parts of SkyBlock into a currency named {{Pink|RNG Meter XP}}. That currency can be put to contribution towards a target of the player choosing, increasing its odds. Upon obtainment of the target, a "price" will be deducted from the stored {{Pink|RNG Meter XP}}.

===Types of RNG Meters===
{{green|5}} types of {{Pink|'''RNG Meters'''}} currently exist, each with their respective ways of contribution:
* {{green|1}} [[File:Experimentation Table.png|21px|link=]][[Experimentation Table]] RNG Meter, from {{Green|0.1%}} of {{Skill|Enchanting}} {{purple|XP}} gained from [[Experiments|Superpairs]] experiments.
* {{green|6}} [[File:Maddox Batphone.png|21px|link=]][[Slayer]] RNG Meters, from {{Pink|Slayer XP}} obtained from killing their respective {{Red|Tier III}} or higher [[Slayer]] bosses.
* {{green|14}} [[File:Mort Skull.png|21px|link=Catacombs]][[Catacombs]] RNG Meters, from {{Aqua|[[Dungeon Score]]}} of completed runs at {{green|70%}} efficiency for {{Gold|S}} or at {{green|100%}} efficiency for {{Gold|S+}}.
* {{green|1}} [[File:Ruby Crystal (v1).png|21px|link=]] [[Crystal Nucleus]] RNG Meter, from {{Blue|Nucleus XP}} of completed [[Crystal Nucleus|Nuclei Runs]], each granting {{Blue|+1000}}.
* {{green|1}} [[File:Vanguard Helmet.png|21px|link=]][[Frozen Corpses]] RNG Meter, from {{Blue|Frozen Corpse XP}} of looted [[Frozen Corpses]], at {{Blue|+500}} per {{Blue|Lapis}} corpse, {{Blue|+2,500}} per {{Gold|Umber}}/{{Gray|Tungsten}} corpse, and {{Blue|+25,000}} per {{Aqua|Vanguard}} corpse.

===RNG Meter Boosts===
{{pink|RNG Meter XP}} can also be increased in the following ways:
* globally, by a flat amount depending on the chosen meter from consuming an {{Item|Ananke Feather}} or an {{Item|RNG Juice}}. The values are listed below.
* globally, by {{Green|1.01→1.10x}} from the {{Attribute|Pity}} attribute ({{Item|Daemon Shard}}). This does not affect {{Item|Ananke Feather}}s nor {{Item|RNG Juice}}.
* on the [[File:Experimentation Table.png|21px|link=]][[Experimentation Table]], by a varying multiplier as {{stat|Enchanting Wisdom}} and other {{Skill|Enchanting}} {{purple|XP}} modifiers directly affect it.

