===Effect of RNG Meter progress on a selected drop===
The formula of the drop rate of an item with the RNG Meter selected is:
::{|class="wikitable"
|<math>
 \text{New Drop Rate} = 
 \text{Base Drop Rate} \times 
     \left(1 + \min
         \left(2 \times \frac
             {\text{Stored }\color{rhodamine}\text{RNG Meter XP} \color{white}}
             {\text{Required } \color{rhodamine} \text{RNG Meter XP}}\right)
             ,2
     \right)
</math>
|}
* If the '''Stored {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''' is above '''Required {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''', then:
**the drop is guaranteed;
**the '''Required {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''' is subtracted from the '''Stored {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}'''.
* In the event a player obtains the targeted drop in its {{Pink|RNG Meter}}:
**If the '''Stored {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''' was below '''Required {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''', then it is reset to {{green|0}}.
** If the '''Stored {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''' was above '''Required {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''', then the '''Required {{pink|RNG Meter XP}}''' is subtracted from it.
* In the event a player obtains a drop that was not targeted in its {{pink|RNG Meter}}:
**the {{pink|RNG Meter}} progress is unaffected.

====In the case of Slayer RNG Meters====
* If a drop has its <math>\text{New Drop Rate} < \color{Green}5\%</math>, then it is increased by {{Stat|Magic Find}}.
*Note that every slayer drop other than guaranteed drops from a full {{pink|RNG Meter}} will display the player's {{Stat|Magic Find}} in the chat message, even if the drop was not actually affected by it.

