== Pity ==
'''{{pink|Pity}}''' is a mechanic that guarantees an event or an item after a task has been repeated a certain number of times. Unlike {{Pink|RNG Meters}} and most of the time:
* there is no currency to be spent;
* there is no choice to be made as {{green|all}} targets are active and are covered by independent counters;
* there is no increase in the drop rate of targets.
* if the player hits the target from luck or {{Pink|Pity}}, its respective counter is reset to {{green|0}}. 
Again, these are not rules set in stone and exceptions occasionally evade them.

Several groups of {{Pink|'''Pity'''}} currently exist, each with their respective ways of contribution:
===Hoppity's Hunt===
After opening {{green|<math>x</math>}} [[Chocolate Rabbits|{{gold|Chocolate Eggs}}]], guarantees the next one to contain a new [[Chocolate Rabbits|{{gold|Chocolate Rabbit}}]] of a given rarity, if available:
*{{Mythic}}: {{LightPurple|250}} [[Chocolate Rabbits|{{gold|Chocolate Eggs}}]]. Subtracts {{Pink|250}} from that counter.
*{{Divine}}: {{Aqua|1,250}} [[Chocolate Rabbits|{{gold|Chocolate Eggs}}]]. Subtracts {{Aqua|1,250}} from that counter. If the player has found all {{Divine}} Rabbits, it guarantees a [[Chocobit Rabbit]] instead.
===Year of the Pig===
After completing {{green|<math>x</math>}} {{Mob|Shiny Pig}}s, guarantees the next one to drop an item.
* {{item|Blood God Crest}}: {{green|1,000}} {{Mob|Shiny Pig}}s
* {{item|Potato Talisman}}: {{green|2,000}} {{Mob|Shiny Pig}}s, both affected by the effect of the {{item|Pig Brain Mixin}}.
===The End===
After {{green|400}} combined {{Mob|Zealot}}s and {{Mob|Zealot Bruiser}}s kills, guarantees the next mob kill to spawn a {{mob|Special Zealot}}.
===Crimson Isle===
*'''[[Trophy Fish]]''': After {{Gold|100}} or {{Aqua|600}} catches of a specific [[Trophy Fish]], guarantees that the next catch will be '''{{Gold|GOLD}}''' or '''{{Aqua|DIAMOND}}''' tier respectively.
*'''[[Vanquisher]]s''': After {{green|750}} kills, guarantees the next one to spawn a {{mob|Vanquisher}}.
===Lotus Atoll===
After {{Gold|100}} or {{Aqua|600}} catches of a specific [[Trophy Frog]], guarantees that the next catch will be of '''{{Gold|GOLD}}''' or '''{{Aqua|DIAMOND}}''' tier respectively. These values are {{green|halved}} for {{Item|Exploding Frog}} and {{Item|Puddle Jumper}}.
===Garden===
* '''[[Spaceman]]''': After {{Green|3,000}} visitors, guarantees that the next visitor will be the {{NPCSprite|Spaceman}}. 
* '''[[Overclocker 3000]]''': {{green|5}} activities increment their respective counter for an {{Item|Overclocker 3000}} : [[Visitors]], [[Jacob's Farming Contests|Jacob's Contests]], [[Crops (disambiguation)|Crops]], [[Greenhouse]], [[Pests]]. The values are only displayed as percentages{{More Info Needed}}.
===Moonglade Marsh===
*After {{Green|1,000}} [[Tree Gifts]], {{Green|2,500}} mob kills, or {{Green|2,500}} [[Treasure|{{gold|treasures}}]] respectively, guarantees the next action to give {{Item|Tree the Fish}}, {{Item|Mob the Fish}}, or {{Item|Swamp the Fish}} respectively.
*Mobs killed in {{Zone|Torrhus Canyon}} also count toward {{Item|Mob the Fish}} progress.
===Torrhus Canyon===
After {{Green|2,500}} [[Treasure|{{gold|treasures}}]], guarantees the next action to give {{Item|Fish the Fish}}.

===Glacite Tunnels===
'''[[Glacite Mineshafts]]''' are a special case as {{Pink|Pity}} works differently: 
*The counter starts from {{Green|2,000}}, decreasing according to the {{gold|Block Quality}} of the block mined. Once the counter reaches {{green|0}}, the next block is guaranteed to spawn a [[Glacite Mineshaft]] portal.
*If a block is mined from {{stat|Mining Spread}} or [[Heart of the Mountain#Pickaxe Abilities|{{AbilityName|Pickobolus}}]], its {{gold|Block Quality}} is {{red|halved}}.
**For example, if a player with {{stat|300 Mining Spread|}} mines a [[File:Packed Ice.png|21px|link=]] [[Glacite]] block, {{green|3}} nearby ones will be indirectly mined. In total, the counter decreases by {{gold|10}}: once by {{gold|4}} and thrice by {{gold|2}}.
* The counter determines the chance of a [[Glacite Mineshaft]] portal spawning on the next block mined: it is the inverse of the counter. 
*{{red|'''However'''}}, on the tab list and in the {{pink|Pity}} menu, the counter appears as starting from {{green|0}}, increasing to {{green|2000}} in contrary to the mechanics initially explained on its introduction<ref>See [[Changelog/2024/April 24]]</ref>
**For example, if the in-game {{Pink|Pity}} counter appears at {{green|859}}, the actual value is {{green|2000-859}}={{green|1141}}. Thus, the probability of spawning a [[Glacite Mineshaft]] portal on the next block is {{chance|0,088%|1|1141|blocks}}.
**For example, if the in-game {{Pink|Pity}} counter appears at {{green|1995}}, the actual value is {{green|2000-1995}}={{green|5}}. Thus, the probability of spawning a [[Glacite Mineshaft]] portal on the next block is {{chance|20%|1|5|blocks}}.

